<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">
  <PropertyGroup>
    <!-- an application, not a library. -->
    <IsPackable>false</IsPackable>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0-android</TargetFramework>
    <OutputType>Exe</OutputType>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <ApplicationId>uk.co.wixely.banter</ApplicationId>
    <ApplicationVersion>1</ApplicationVersion>
    <!-- The version people see, from the one place the repository's version lives. It was
         hardcoded 0.1.0 and had been wrong since the day the repo moved past it - the same
         staleness that the CI package version had. CI overrides both this and ApplicationVersion
         on a tag. -->
    <ApplicationDisplayVersion>$(VersionPrefix)</ApplicationDisplayVersion>
    <SupportedOSPlatformVersion>26</SupportedOSPlatformVersion>
    <RootNamespace>Banter.App.Android</RootNamespace>
    <!--
      CoreCLR, and this is load-bearing rather than a preference: the Mono runtime pack in .NET 10
      (10.0.11) has a code-generation defect that kills a CupriFace app during startup. It is a
      native SIGSEGV inside Mono-compiled CoreLib where string CONTENT is dereferenced as a string
      REFERENCE, and it reproduces on arm64 hardware and x64 emulators alike, AOT and JIT alike
      (they share the code generator), trimmed or not. CupriFace's own forensics are in
      samples/AndroidProbe/MONO-CRASH.md.

      Set HERE and not left to the CupriFace.Android package, which does try: its buildTransitive
      targets carry `UseMonoRuntime Condition="'$(UseMonoRuntime)' == ''"`, and for an Android app
      that condition is never true — the Android SDK has already set it to `true` by the time a
      NuGet .targets file is imported, so the default cannot fire and the pin silently does
      nothing. Measured on 0.24.1: `-getProperty:UseMonoRuntime` answered `true` and the APK
      shipped libmonosgen-2.0.so. The first build that ever reached a device crashed in OnCreate.

      It costs size, and more than the per-ABI figures suggest: this APK went from 26 MB to 49 MB,
      because it carries arm64-v8a AND x86_64 and both runtimes doubled. Dropping the emulator ABI
      would halve it, which is worth doing when this is something people download rather than
      something we sideload. Re-evaluate the whole pin when the Mono pack moves past 10.0.11.
    -->
    <UseMonoRuntime>false</UseMonoRuntime>
  </PropertyGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="../Banter.App/Banter.App.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="../Banter.Voice.OpenAI/Banter.Voice.OpenAI.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="../Banter.Voice.Wyoming/Banter.Voice.Wyoming.csproj" />
    <PackageReference Include="CupriFace.Android" Version="0.24.1" />
  </ItemGroup>
</Project>
